  "questionnaireDesign": {
    "note": "Planning note for the six-language Client Portal questionnaire. Not implemented as UI here -- this documents the agreed contract the PDF generation logic above already honors.",
    "tripEntries": "Repeatable block, exactly 3 instances (matching the PDF's 3 physical rows): Arrival Date, Arrival Flight Number, Departure Date, Departure Flight Number. Each field labelled in the client's preferred language per the existing pattern -- official English label first, translation in parentheses, e.g. \"Arrival Date (입국일자)\".",
    "additionalTravelHistory": "A separate, single free-text field (not a 4th structured entry, since the PDF has no 4th row): \"If you need to report more than three trips, describe them here for FIS staff to arrange separately.\" Routed to staff for manual handling (e.g. a supplementary note, or splitting across multiple requests) -- never auto-inserted onto the 3-row grid, and never silently dropped.",
    "courtLegalConditional": "Implements the approved conditional logic: \"Are you requesting your travel records for court proceedings or another legal purpose?\" Yes/No. YES reveals Name of Court / Branch-Place / Court Contact Number as customer input for staff review; NO hides them. Either way the official PDF's Court/Legal section remains staff-controlled -- the questionnaire answer informs staff, it does not write directly to the form."
